<%
  page_data(
    title: "Exchange authorisation code for access token",
    error: false,
    caption: "API developer documentation",
    caption_size: 'l'
  )
%>

<p class="govuk-body">
When you receive the authorisation code, you must exchange it for an access token within 10 minutes. This continues from the
<%= govuk_link_to("receive authorisation results",
                  api_documentation_authorisation_page_path("receive-authorisation-results"),
                  no_visited_state: true) %> step.
</p>

<%#
  Mermaid code for the image

sequenceDiagram
    actor User as Client
    participant Vendor as Application
    participant RIAB as Authorisation API

    Vendor->>RIAB: POST /oauth/token
    RIAB->>RIAB: Validate request and generate token
    RIAB-->>Vendor: 200 OK with token payload
%>

<%= image_tag("documentation/authorisation/exchange-code-for-token.png", width: "700px", alt: "Exchange authorisation code for access token sequence diagram") %>

<h4 class="govuk-heading-s">What the diagram shows</h4>

<ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
  <li>Your application sends a POST request to /oauth/token on the authorisation API.</li> 
  <li>The authorisation API validates the request and generates a token. </li> 
  <li>The authorisation API returns 200 OK with the token payload.</li> 
</ol>

<h4 class="govuk-heading-s">Send the request</h4>

<p class="govuk-body">
Send an HTTP POST request to our token endpoint.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
You must authenticate the request using <%= govuk_link_to("HTTP Basic Authentication", "https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc7617/") %>
with your client ID and client secret.  To do this, add an HTTP header containing your credentials in the form <code>client_id:client_secret</code>, Base64 encoded.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
For example, if your client ID is <code>client123</code> and your secret is <code>supersecretvalue</code>, your Basic Authentication header would be:

<pre>
<code>
Authorization: Basic Y2xpZW50MTIzOnN1cGVyc2VjcmV0dmFsdWU=
</code>
</pre>

</p>

<%= govuk_warning_text(text: "Do not include your client ID or client secret in the body of the request.") %>


<p class="govuk-body">
Put the other parameters in the request body, not in additional request headers.
</p>


<%= govuk_table do |table|
  table.with_head do |head|
    head.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "Parameter")
      row.with_cell(text: "Description")
    end
  end
  table.with_body do |body|
    body.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "<code>grant_type</code>".html_safe)
      row.with_cell(text: "The OAuth 2.0 grant type. The only value we currently accept is <code>authorization_code</code>.".html_safe)
    end
    body.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "<code>redirect_uri</code>".html_safe)
      row.with_cell(text: "The redirect URI you used when you called the authorisation endpoint.")
    end
    body.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "<code>code</code>".html_safe)
      row.with_cell(text: "The authorisation code we sent you in the previous step.")
    end
    body.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "<code>code_verifier</code>".html_safe)
      row.with_cell(text: "Your #{govuk_link_to("PKCE", "https://oauth.net/2/pkce/")} <code>code_verifier</code>.".html_safe)
    end
  end
end %>

<h4 class="govuk-heading-s">Example request</h4>

<pre>
<code>
  curl -X POST <%= @api_base_url %>/oauth/token \
  --user "client123:supersecretvalue" \
  -H "content-type:application/x-www-form-urlencoded" \
  --data \
  "grant_type=authorization_code\
  &redirect_uri=[YOUR-REDIRECT-URI]\
  &code=[AUTHORIZATION-CODE] \
  &code_verifier=[CODE-VERIFIER]"
</code>
</pre>
<h4 class="govuk-heading-s">Example response</h4>

<p class="govuk-body">
If the request is successful, we return HTTP status 201 to show your token was created. The response includes a JSON payload containing the access token.
</p>

<pre>
<code>
{
  "access_token": "QGbWG8KckncuwwD4uYXgWxF4HQvuPmrmUqKgkpQP",
  "token_type": "Bearer",
  "expires_in": 31536000
}
</code>
</pre>

<p class="govuk-body">
The access token works like a password. It gives you access to the API as the organisation that authorised the request, so you must store it securely. 
</p>

<h4 class="govuk-heading-s">Error responses</h4>

<p class="govuk-body">
If the request is unsuccessful, we return an HTTP error status and a JSON payload containing an error value. For example:
</p>

<pre>
<code>
{
  error: "invalid_grant"
}
</code>
</pre>

<%= govuk_table do |table|
  table.with_head do |head|
    head.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "Error scenario")
      row.with_cell(text: "HTTP status")
      row.with_cell(text: "Error code")
    end
  end
  table.with_body do |body|
    body.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "Client ID or client secret is invalid")
      row.with_cell(text: "401 (Unauthorized)")
      row.with_cell(text: "invalid_client")
    end
    body.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "Grant type is missing")
      row.with_cell(text: "400 (Bad Request)")
      row.with_cell(text: "invalid_request")
    end
    body.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "Grant type is invalid")
      row.with_cell(text: "400 (Bad Request)")
      row.with_cell(text: "unsupported_grant_type")
    end
    body.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "Redirect URI is missing")
      row.with_cell(text: "400 (Bad Request)")
      row.with_cell(text: "invalid_grant")
    end
    body.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "Redirect URI is invalid")
      row.with_cell(text: "400 (Bad Request)")
      row.with_cell(text: "invalid_grant")
    end
    body.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "Code is missing")
      row.with_cell(text: "400 (Bad Request)")
      row.with_cell(text: "invalid_grant")
    end
    body.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "Code is invalid")
      row.with_cell(text: "400 (Bad Request)")
      row.with_cell(text: "invalid_grant")
    end
    body.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "Code verifier is missing")
      row.with_cell(text: "400 (Bad Request)")
      row.with_cell(text: "invalid_grant")
    end
    body.with_row do |row|
      row.with_cell(text: "Code verifier is invalid")
      row.with_cell(text: "400 (Bad Request)")
      row.with_cell(text: "invalid_grant")
    end
  end
end %>
